# `__eq__` and `__hash__` ⚖️

By default, `user1 == user2` is only True if they are the *exact same object in memory*.

If you want them to be equal if their IDs match, override `__eq__`.
If you want to use your custom object as a Dictionary Key, you MUST override `__hash__`!

```python_not
class User:
    # ... (init from previous slide)

    def __eq__(self, other) -> bool:
        if isinstance(other, User):
            return self.uid == other.uid
        return False

    def __hash__(self) -> int:
        # Hash based on the unique ID
        return hash(self.uid)
```
